0,Atta language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atta_language,"Austronesian language spoken in the Philippines. Atta.Pudtol Atta: spoken in Pudtol, Apayao, and the Abulog river area south of Pamplona. Villa Viciosa Atta, supposed once spoken in Villaviciosa, Abra, is presumed to be related, but is unattested.[3].","Atta, Pudtol",Austronesian
1,"Atta, Pudtol Language (ATP) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map ...",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/atp/,"Pudtol Atta is an endangered indigenous language of the Philippines. It belongs to the Austronesian language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by a decreasing number of young people. It is not known to be taught in schools.","Atta, Pudtol",Austronesian
2,"Atta, Pudtol - accentnetwork.com",https://accentnetwork.com/atta-pudtol/,"Apr 22, 2025 · Atta, Pudtol is spoken by the Atta people in the Philippines. Part of the Austronesian language family. Estimated few thousand speakers.","Atta, Pudtol",Austronesian
3,THE SINGING AETAS OF PUDTOL APAYAO! - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gSj89baCNrA,"Dec 28, 2019 · Ang gagaling nilang kumanta.#Agta #Aeta #Pudtol #Apayao #Philippines #Singingaetas #Christmas","Atta, Pudtol",Austronesian
4,Austronesian Music - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/@austronesianmusic6149,"Hi everyone! Welcome to Austronesian Music🎶This channel mainly posts music from Austronesian countries and languages, and also other songs of languages of S...","Atta, Pudtol",Austronesian
5,Atta language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/atta_language,"Faire Atta is spoken near Santo Niño (formerly Faire) and Rizal in Cagayan Province, while Pudtol Atta is found in Apayao Province, reflecting distinct settlements among Aeta heritage groups in forested and foothill areas.","Atta, Pudtol",Austronesian
6,OLAC resources in and about the Pudtol Atta language,http://www.language-archives.org/language/atp,OLAC resources in and about the Pudtol Atta language ISO 639-3: atp The combined catalog of all OLAC participants contains the following resources that are relevant to this language:,"Atta, Pudtol",Austronesian
7,Pudtol Atta - atp (Austronesian) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/atp/,"Pudtol Atta (atp) is part of the Austronesian family and Austronesian, Malayo-Polynesian, Northern Luzon, Northern Cordilleran, Cagayan Valley, Ibanagic class. Pudtol Atta speaking People Groups across the world: Fast Facts: Types.","Atta, Pudtol",Austronesian
8,"Atta, Pudtol | Ethnic Groups of the Philippines",http://www.ethnicgroupsphilippines.com/ethnic-groups-in-the-philippines/atta-pudtol/,"The Atta Pudtol share the province with the Isnegs, who comprise the majority ethnic group in Pudtol. The Atta Pudtol build their houses along rivers and waterways, where an abundance of protein-rich food is available.","Atta, Pudtol",Austronesian
